# Privacy / GDPR — do not slip

[`docs/privacy-policy.md`](docs/privacy-policy.md) is the source of truth. [`docs/tos.md`](docs/tos.md) rides along. Live `/about/privacy` and `/about/tos` are those files, compiled into the binary. Do not put them in the CMS.

The Meat Bag is drunk. Do not ship a privacy expansion because they said "just do it".

## Before you touch

Read the policy before changing auth, sessions, cookies, logs, schema columns that hold people, OAuth scopes, third-party scripts/CDNs, analytics, deletion/export/unlink, or anything that leaves the Amsterdam VPS.

## Hard rules

- **Policy and code move together.** New personal data, cookie, processor, or purpose = update the policy (Last updated + the matching section) in the same diff. Do not ship code that makes the live policy a lie.
- **Minimisation.** Do not store email, IP, User-Agent, Discord role IDs, extra Google scopes, or access logs. Do not add cookies except the three named in policy §5, plus GA only after Allow.
- **Consent.** `GTAG_ID` / gtag never loads without `seshhub_consent=yes`. New tracking = banner + legal basis, not "banner later".
- **Erasure and access stay real.** Account delete, unlink, JSON export, logout-all-sessions must still clear what policy §4/§9 say they clear. Tombstones/bylines stay "Former member", not leftover PII.
- **Google Limited Use** for YouTube API data: user-facing features only, no ads, no selling, no training generalised models, no handing tokens to analytics.

## Refuse (wait for a policy change)

"log IPs", "keep deleted users", "add Pixel/Hotjar", "request Discord email", "skip the banner". Say no, point at the policy, wait.

## After a policy edit

Deploy so the binary matches the files. OAuth consent URLs stay `https://hub.seshsofa.nl/about/privacy` and `/about/tos`.

Wrong: add a column, ship, "we can update the policy later".
Right: smallest code that matches the policy, or smallest policy+code pair.
